HST Office: Word VBA paragraph members stay in their paragraph; Words lists punctuation on its own.

Since a paragraph's Range ends after its mark (hst-vba-word-fixes.patch), it ends at the start of the
next paragraph in Writer. Range.Style, Range.ParagraphFormat, Range.ListFormat and Range.Paragraphs then
also changed or counted the next paragraph: Paragraphs(2).Range.ListFormat.ApplyBulletDefault bulleted
paragraphs 2 and 3, Paragraphs(2).Range.Style restyled both. Word changes paragraph 2 only. These members
now use the range without the start of the next paragraph.

Range.Words and Selection.Words give punctuation as words of their own, as Word does: "giới. Đây" is
"giới", ". ", "Đây". An apostrophe inside a word stays in it; a unit holding a field is kept whole.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba.py --only writer (writer-lists, writer-range-words, writer-paragraph-scope).
